    <interactorList>      <interactor id="101">
        <names>
          <shortLabel>VOZ2</shortLabel>
          <fullName>Transcription factor VOZ2; Transcriptional activator acting positively in the phytochrome B signaling pathway. Functions redundantly with VOZ1 to promote flowering downstream of phytochrome B (phyB). Down-regulates &#x27;FLOWERING LOCUS C&#x27; (FLC) and up-regulates &#x27;FLOWERING LOCUS T&#x27; (FT). Binds to the 38-bp cis-acting region of the AVP1 gene. Binds as a dimer to the palindromic sequence 5&#x27;-GCGTNNNNNNNACGC-3&#x27;. Interacts with phyB in the cytoplasm and is translocated to the nucleus at signal transmission, where it is subjected to degradation in a phytochrome- dependent manner.</fullName>
